{"id": "EUVD-2026-59273", "enisaUuid": "1db7cd92-5e28-3cfb-a684-2a70e42178cf", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nafs: Fix callback service message parsers to pass through -EAGAIN\n\nThe AFS filesystem client uses an rxrpc server to listen for callback\nnotifications.  Each callback call type handler has a delivery function\nthat parses the incoming request stream, and this should return -EAGAIN the\nlast packet hasn't yet been seen, but all currently queued received data is\nconsumed.  afs_extract_data() does this, but the -EAGAIN return is switched\nto 0 inadvertantly\n\nFix callback service message parsers to pass through -EAGAIN", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:56:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:55:20", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/26b737b3769e92493fe94c34620399d93ca231ae", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/09c67a7ded481482155b836c8c7f078a3075f8de", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/239cd337c9d047e7097f5b2ebbb41ddfb8180bc6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5a39b145a8fb49f316e7ec1f29ba51d68095c7e4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/772850871a2e772e26f9d93f1e9ddd413b3eeaa4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0acbc09d2aca0432af45cec114f20d55ceafaec4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f14dd036fad3d359f26f1282199cec06b3a9362b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0f36469d7ce98b362934113c550d08bb0c784231"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-72374", "GHSA-82qr-pqhc-837w"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.72, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c0aada9-c66a-3310-a2bc-e1580d79217a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d001648ec7cf8b21ae9eec8b9ba4a18295adfb14 <0acbc09d2aca0432af45cec114f20d55ceafaec4"}, {"id": "13aae6aa-42ed-3728-9a8e-359e6f943607", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.9"}, {"id": "1413ef22-e766-33c3-879a-6c90bd